        "a": "It covers the descriptive part of bibliometrics: output per year, top topics, sources, authors and institutions, open-access share and the most-cited works. It does not build co-authorship or co-citation networks, compute indicators such as the h-index, or let you download the records. For that, use dedicated bibliometric software on an exported dataset."
